 671            /
 672            /       HERE BEGINS THE DISPLAY CALCULATIONS FOR THE TWO SHIPS.  AT
 673            /       THIS POINT ONLY THE POSITION AND ORIENTATION OF EACH VESSEL
 674            /       IS ONF INTEREST SINCE THE VELOCITY AND ALL THAT HAVE ALREADY
 675            /       BEEN TAKEN CARE OF.  FOR THE BOTH SHIPS THE DISPLAY FILES ARE
 676            /       CALCULATED AS A SERIES OF PAIRS OF X,Y COORDINATES.  BETWEEN
 677            /       EACH PAIR OF POINTS A FOUR POINT VECTOR WILL BE DRAWN.  THE
 678            /       ACTUAL COORDINATES ARE CALCULATED AS DISPLACEMENTS
 679            /       FROM THE CENTRAL PSOTION OF THE SHIP, TAKING INTO ACCOUNT THE
 680            /       ANGLE OF ORIENTATION.  THE FORMULAS FOLLOWED ARE:
 681            /
 682            /       X(POINT)=X(BASE)+X(REL)*COS[THE]+Y(REL)*SINE[THE]
 683            /
 684            /       Y(POINT)=Y(BASE)+Y(REL)*COS[THE]-X(REL)*SINE[THE]
 685            /
 686            /       WHERE SINE[THE] AND COS[THE] ARE THE FUNCTIONS OF THE
 687            /       ANGLE OF ORIENTATION, X(BASE) AND Y(BASE) ARE THE 
 688            /       COORDINATES OF THE SHIPS POSITION AND X(REL) AND Y(REL)
 689            /       CORRESPOND TO DISPLACEMENT PAIRS DEPENDING ON THE SHAPE
 690            /       OF THE FIGURE.  ALL X AND Y RELS LIE WITHIN THE RANGE 0-3 AND
 691            /       THERE FORE ALL NECESSARY DISPLACEMENTS FROM BASE COORDINATES
 692            /       MAY BE CALCULATEDFROM DIFFERENT COMBINATIONS OF T10SIN, T20COS
 693            /       ETC.  THESE VALUES ARE CALCULATED BY A CALL TO POSCAL WITH THE SINE 
 694            /       AND COSINE OF THE ANGLE OF INTEREST IN CALSIN AND CALCOS.
 695            /
 696            /       FOLLOWING THIS METHOD ANY FIGURE DESCRIBABLE WITH A 7 BY 7
 697            /       MATRIX OF POINTS MAY BE QUICKLY CALCULATED.
 698            /
 699            /       BEGINNING AT ONESET DIFFERENT DISPLACEMENT PAIRS ARE CALCULATED
 700            /       AND DEPOSITIED THROUGH AUTO10 TO FORM THE DISPLAY FILE FOR SHIP NUMBER ONE.
 701            /
 702            
 703            
 704                    *1000
 705            
 706 01000 7300 ONESET, CLA CLL                 /BEGIN DISPLAY FILE FOR NUMBER ONE
 707 01001 1022         TAD ONEFLG              /DONT BOTHER IF NOT IN NORMAL SPACE
 708 01002 7640         SZA CLA
 709 01003 5753         JMP I ITWOST
 710 01004 1030         TAD ONESIN              /SET UP FOR MATRIX COMPONENT CALCULATIONS
 711 01005 3063         DCA CALSIN
 712 01006 1031         TAD ONECOS
 713 01007 3064         DCA CALCOS
 714 01010 4472         JMS I CALPOS            /CALL THE CALCULATOR
